        "title": "Organizational Psychology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Industrial-Organizational (I-O) psychology applies psychological science to work\ncontexts. It has the most rigorous empirical tradition in applied psychology —\nSchmidt and Hunter's meta-analytic work on selection validity is among the\nmost policy-relevant research in social science. If you hire people, lead teams,\nor design work systems, this field's findings directly apply."
